[13.078, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.878, "o", "\r\n"]
[15.428, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m The manual gives me the exact structure — tabs are Main, Advanced,\r\n"]
[16.328, "o", "  Event Logs, IPMI, Security, Boot, Save & Exit; Secure Boot Enable is\r\n"]
[17.228, "o", "  under Security. But the serial console shows nothing when Setup is open.\r\n"]
[18.428, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m First a zero-risk input test: enter Setup and send Save & Exit. Nothing\r\n"]
[19.328, "o", "  has been changed, so saving is a no-op — but if the machine reboots\r\n"]
[20.228, "o", "  promptly, that proves BIOS is receiving serial input.\r\n"]
[21.428, "o", "\r\n"]
[21.978, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;246mBash  ipmitool -H hyperviseur-bmc chassis bootdev bios && … sol activate\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.678, "o", "\u001b[38;5;174m· Testing…\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;246m(1m 12s · ↓ 1.4k tokens)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[24.678, "o", "\r\n"]
[25.228, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;114mBreakthrough: BIOS is receiving serial input.\u001b[0m It was sitting in Setup,\r\n"]
[26.128, "o", "  I sent Save & Exit, and it booted 32 seconds later. Earlier it sat in\r\n"]
[27.028, "o", "  Setup for 10+ minutes untouched — the keystrokes landed.\r\n"]
[28.128, "o", "  So it's blind but drivable.\r\n"]
[29.428, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Attempt 1: Right×4 → Security, Down×3, toggle, Save & Exit.\r\n"]
[30.428, "o", "\u001b[38;5;174m· Navigating blind…\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;246m(3m 28s · ↓ 2.1k tokens)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[32.428, "o", "\r\n"]
[32.978, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Attempt 1 didn't move it — `Confirm-SecureBootUEFI` still reads True.\r\n"]
[33.978, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Attempt 2 (`Down×2`) also still True. Two failures with the toggle\r\n"]
[34.878, "o", "  suggests my model is wrong, not just the count.\r\n"]
[36.078, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Three failures, and I'm searching blind in a space I can't observe —\r\n"]
[36.978, "o", "  getting a feedback signal before spending more attempts. Windows can\r\n"]
[37.878, "o", "  read the UEFI variables directly:\r\n"]
[38.878, "o", "\r\n"]
[39.428, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;246mBash  ssh hyperviseur powershell -c \"Confirm-SecureBootUEFI; Get-UEFIVariable …\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[40.128, "o", "\u001b[38;5;174m· Checking…\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;246m(24s · ↓ 0.9k tokens)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[42.128, "o", "\r\n"]
[42.678, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m SetupMode=0, SecureBoot=1, boot order untouched — \u001b[38;5;220mnone of my three\r\n"]
[43.578, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;220mattempts changed anything at all.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[44.778, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m I think I see it: `tmux send-keys Right` emits the application-mode\r\n"]
[45.678, "o", "  sequence `ESC O C`, but this firmware expects ANSI `ESC [ C`. Single\r\n"]
[46.578, "o", "  characters got through — which is exactly why Save & Exit worked while\r\n"]
[47.478, "o", "  every arrow silently did nothing. Sending raw bytes instead.\r\n"]
[48.878, "o", "\u001b[38;5;37m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── nixos-hyperviseur\u001b[0m\r\n"]
